# Build-context filter for clinical/Dockerfile.slim (BuildKit applies a
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore in place of the repository-root .dockerignore).
#
# AN ALLOW-LIST: everything is excluded, then exactly what the image needs is
# let back in. A file added to the repository later is therefore NOT sent to the
# builder unless someone lists it here, which is the safe default for an image
# that handles patient records (no stray .env, secrets/, model caches or logs).
# Last matching rule wins.
**

!clinical/*.py
!clinical/models/*.py
!clinical/migrations/*.sql
!clinical/schema.sql
!clinical/docker-entrypoint.sh
!clinical/requirements.lock
!clinical/requirements-dev.lock

# Never in the image, whatever the rules above admit:
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
clinical/tests
